  "instructions": [
    "Preheat grill to 275°F (135°C).",
    "In a small bowl, whisk together hoisin sauce, bhuna curry paste, brown sugar, apple cider vinegar, honey, water, salt, black pepper, garlic powder, and paprika to make the glaze.",
    "Remove the membrane from the back of the pork ribs and season with salt and black pepper.",
    "Place the ribs on the grill and cook for 2 hours, or until they reach an internal temperature of 160°F (71°C).",
    "After 2 hours, brush the ribs with the glaze every 10 minutes for the next 30 minutes, or until the ribs are caramelized and the glaze is set.",
    "Remove the ribs from the grill and let them rest for 10 minutes before serving.",
    "Garnish with chopped fresh parsley, if desired.",
    "Serve immediately and enjoy!"
  ],
